		<article id="kaggle-competition">
			<h3>Kaggle Competition: LLM Mathematical Reasoning</h3>
			<p><strong>Type:</strong> Machine Learning and LLM Inference</p>
			<p>This project focused on improving the mathematical reasoning performance of Qwen3-4B-Thinking, a four-billion-parameter inference model. We worked under the constraints that we could not fine-tune the model weights or use external tools.</p>
			<p>We designed a string-level post-processing module that handled brace matching, merged multiple <code>\boxed</code> expressions, and separated coordinate-style answers. These changes increased our Kaggle public leaderboard accuracy from 46.9% to 62.5% without requiring additional GPU computation.</p>
			<p>We also created a fixed validation and ablation-testing framework to support later self-consistency sampling experiments. During the competition, our team briefly reached first place on the public leaderboard.</p>
			<p><strong>Technologies:</strong> Python, vLLM, PyTorch, Prompt Engineering, Self-Consistency Sampling, Kaggle</p>
